\title{Memory Tiling (GPU)}

\p{An example of how to tile a matrix multiplication, our tile partitions the output matrix #{M \times N} by block sizes \code{BS_N} and \code{BS_M} as seen in the image below (drawn using excalidraw)}
\figure{
\<html:img>[width]{80\%}[src]{\route-asset{assets/img/tiled-matmul.png}}{}
\figcaption{Tiling with dimensions}
}
\p{The block size of #{k} \code{BS_K} is then basically the \em{accumulation axis}, where we loop over #{k} if we cannot fit the whole row / column of #{A} and #{B} into [shared memory](8GZN).}
